This crate (`symphonia-codec-ralf`) is a from-scratch, pure-Rust RealAudio Lossless (RALF) decoder.
It is licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

RALF has no public specification. The block and packet layout, the entropy coding (including the
canonical assignment of codes to the code length tables), the prediction filter and the stereo
reconstruction follow FFmpeg's `libavcodec/ralf.c`, and the code length tables in `src/tables.rs`
(extracted programmatically) are those of `libavcodec/ralfdata.h`. FFmpeg is distributed under the
GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.

